<!doctype html><html lang=en><head><script data-cfasync=false src=https://transcend-cdn.com/cm/fa619274-3c15-4155-bbec-c0cb75733259/airgap.js></script><meta charset=utf-8><meta name=viewport content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,maximum-scale=5,user-scalable=yes"><meta http-equiv=X-UA-Compatible content="IE=edge, chrome=1"><meta name=theme-color content="#1a8cff"><link rel=alternate hreflang=x-default href=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/><link rel=alternate hreflang=en-US href=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/><link rel=alternate hreflang=en-CA href=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/><link rel=alternate hreflang=en-GB href=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/><link rel=alternate hreflang=en-AU href=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/><link rel=alternate hreflang=en-NZ href=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/><link rel=alternate hreflang=en-IN href=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/><link rel=manifest href=/site.webmanifest><meta name=msapplication-config content="/browserconfig.xml"><link rel=icon href=/favicon.ico type=image/x-icon media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)"><link rel=icon href=/favicon-light.ico type=image/x-icon media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"><link rel=icon href=/img/favicon/icon-v2.svg type=image/svg+xml media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)"><link rel=icon href=/img/favicon/icon-v2-light.svg type=image/svg+xml media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"><link rel=apple-touch-icon href=/img/favicon/apple-touch-icon-v2.png><link rel=mask-icon href=/img/favicon/pinned-tab-v2.svg color=black><script src=/gtag-production.4d7b82e97bcbe525fb69c6dcde50d003.js async></script><link rel=stylesheet type=text/css href=/compiled-tailwind.a0845612189712c95477cbf9f724e514.css><script src=/react-components.bundle.41ecb078339800cf4589c8d6c4fb2bcf.js async></script><script type=application/ld+json>{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"1Password","alternateName":"AgileBits Inc.","founders":[{"@type":"Person","name":"Roustem Karimov","sameAs":"https://twitter.com/roustem"},{"@type":"Person","name":"Dave Teare","sameAs":"https://twitter.com/dteare"}],"employee":[{"@type":"Person","name":"Jeff Shiner","jobTitle":"CEO","sameAs":"https://twitter.com/jeffreyshiner"}],"foundingDate":"2006","knowsAbout":[{"@type":"Thing","name":"Online Security"},{"@type":"Thing","name":"Password Management"},{"@type":"Thing","name":"1Password extension"}],"awards":["Mac App Store: Best of 2013","Macworld: Eddy Awards 2013 Winner","MacGadka & MyApple: Product of the Year 2013","iTunes: Best of 2014","iMore: Best of 2014","Apple: Best of 2015 and 2016","Embarcadero: Coolest App contest 2016","Android Central: Best Password Manager 2017","IT Pro: Best Apps of 2017","Today: Coolest Apps of 2017","Wirecutter: Best Password Manager","Ars Technica: Design Award","Mac Format: Choice Award"],"numberOfEmployees":"100+","parentOrganization":"AgileBits Inc.","Address":{"streetAddress":"4711 Yonge St, 10th Floor","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","postalCode":"M2N 6K8 ","addressCountry":"Canada"},"description":"1Password remembers your passwords all for you. Save your passwords and log in to sites with a single click. It’s that simple.","disambiguatingDescription":"1Password: Password Manager for Teams, Families, Businesses","url":"https://1password.com/","logo":"https:\/\/releases.1password.com\/img\/logo-v1-min.png","sameAs":["https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/1Password","https://www.facebook.com/1Password","https://twitter.com/1Password","https://www.linkedin.com/company/1Password","https://vimeo.com/1password","https://www.youtube.com/1PasswordVideos","https://www.instagram.com/1password/","https://github.com/1Password","https://www.reddit.com/r/1Password/"]}</script><link rel=preload href=/fonts/averta-op-regular-v1.woff2 as=font type=font/woff2 crossorigin=anonymous><link rel=preload href=/fonts/averta-op-bold-v1.woff2 as=font type=font/woff2 crossorigin=anonymous><link rel=stylesheet href="/css/bundle.f6902eb29e494903505ebfd9cc865398.css" type=text/css><title>1Password CLI | 1Password Releases</title><script type=text/javascript src=/js/bundle.a90c44ab2727c9749c7c96649ad13b18.js async></script><script type=text/javascript src=/js/analytics.bundle.a8d082268ee98af494685eca0b6c5e67.js async></script><meta property="og:image" content="https://releases.1password.com/img/og-image-default-v2.png"><meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="https://releases.1password.com/img/og-image-default-v2.png"><meta name=twitter:image content="https://releases.1password.com/img/og-image-default-v2.png"><meta name=twitter:card content="summary_large_image"><meta property="og:title" content="1Password CLI | 1Password Releases"><meta name=twitter:title content="1Password CLI | 1Password Releases"><meta name=twitter:site content="@1Password"><meta name=twitter:creator content="@1Password"><meta property="og:description" content="All the latest releases from the 1Password team"><meta name=description content="All the latest releases from the 1Password team"><meta name=twitter:description content="All the latest releases from the 1Password team"></head><body><a class=skip-link href=#main-content tabindex=0>Skip to Main Content</a><nav id=navbar class="nav-experiment-old js-offset-navbar brand-primary-dark-bar"><div class="c-browser-banner u-p-2"><img src=/img/redesign/browser-banner-warning.png alt="Your browser is out of date" class="o-image u-is-displayinlineblock u-mr-2 c-browser-banner__icon">
Your browser is out of date. For the best experience, upgrade your browser now.</div><div class=navigation id=navigation><a href=https://1password.com/ class="logo-container logo-container--center" data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=home_logo data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/><img src=/img/1password-logo-mobile-light@2x.png class=logo alt=1Password>
</a><button id=menu-button aria-haspopup=true>Menu</button><ul class="burger c-unleash-experiment" aria-labelledby=menu-button><li class=nav-home><a href=https://1password.com/ class=current data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=home data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Home</a></li><li><a href=https://1password.com/tour/ data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=tour data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Tour</a></li><li><a href=https://1password.com/families/ data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=families data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Families</a></li><li><a href=https://1password.com/business/ data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=business data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Business</a></li><li><a href=https://1password.com/developers/ class=current data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=developers data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Developers</a></li><li><a href=https://1password.com/teams/pricing/ class=js-override-teams-link data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=pricing data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Pricing</a></li><li><a href=https://1password.com/security/ data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=security data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Security</a></li><li data-unleash-conditional-render=experiment_nav_bar_download class=download-hidden><a href=https://1password.com/downloads/ data-event-category=Signups data-event-action=download data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Download</a></li><li><a href=https://support.1password.com/ data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=support data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Support</a></li><li><a href=https://blog.1password.com/ data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=blog data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Blog</a></li><li class=mobile-only><a href="https://start.1password.com/signin?l=en" data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=sign_in data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Sign in</a></li></ul><div class=signup-container><ul><li class=signin><a id=dynamic-signin-link href="https://start.1password.com/signin?l=en" class=signin data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=sign_in data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Sign in</a></li><li class="buy signup"><a class=js-override-teams-link href=https://1password.com/teams/pricing/ data-event-category=nav_click data-event-action=try_1password_free data-event-label=https://releases.1password.com/developers/cli/>Try 1Password FREE</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><main id=main-content tabindex=-1><section class="c-panel c-panel--text-center c-panel--brand-primary-dark u-pt-16 u-pt-20@md u-is-displayflex"><div class="c-panel__container u-full-width u-max-width-md@md u-px-0@md"><header><div class="c-author u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-flexvertical u-text-sm u-mb-2 u-mb-4@md"><a class="c-heading c-heading--1 u-mb-6 u-mt-4 c-heading--light" href=../><h1 class="c-heading c-heading--1 u-mb-6 u-mt-4 c-heading--light">1Password CLI</h1></a><div class="u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter"><div class="c-author__name c-author__name--release">by Simon</div><img src=/img/authors/simon.f3dcb3e4456ac8997dca103ddf332682.jpg srcset="/img/authors/simon@2x.441f506ff005c0753d2852b154bcbdbb.jpg 2x" class="o-image c-author__photo c-author__photo--release u-mr-4" alt=Simon></div><div class="c-page-details c-page-details--release c-page-details--release@sm u-text-left u-is-displayflex@sm u-aligncenter@sm u-mb-0 u-px-4 u-py-4"><div class="u-flexgrow u-text-left">Updated to 2.42.0 on<time datetime="2026-11-04 00:00:00 +0000 UTC">&nbsp;November 4, 2026</time></div><a href=https://releases.1password.com/developers/ class="c-icon c-icon--developers c-icon--platform u-is-displayinlineflex u-is-displayflex@sm u-flexhorizontal u-mt-2 u-mt-0@sm u-mb-0"><img src=/img/icons/developers.fab48e710e4e03a77f238bd042573bc9.svg class="o-image u-mr-2" alt>
Developer tools</a></div></div></header></div></section><section class="c-panel u-pt-20"><div class="c-panel__container c-panel--max-width@md u-px-0@md u-pb-4 u-pb-12@md content"><a href=https://www.1password.dev/cli/get-started class="c-button u-mb-8">Download 1Password CLI</a><p><a href=https://www.1password.dev/cli/get-started>1Password CLI</a> 2.42.0 is now available. 🎉</p><p>This release adds <code>op environment secret list</code>, which lists the name and value of each secret in a 1Password Environment. It also adds a collection of new shell plugins and fixes how <code>op item get</code>, <code>op read</code>, <code>op run</code>, and <code>op inject</code> handle addresses when some parts are empty.</p><p>Subscribe to the <a href=/developers/cli/index.xml>RSS feed</a> for 1Password CLI release notes.</p><hr><span id=changelog class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</span><div class=u-is-displayflex@sm><h3 class="c-heading u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-flexgrow" id=whats-new><span class="c-icon fal fa-sync c-icon--updates u-mr-4 u-mb-0"></span><a href=#whats-new class="anchor u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-z-10 u-flexgrow">What's new</a></h3><button class="c-icon c-icon--gitlab-large u-is-displayinlineflex u-flexhorizontal u-alignself-start u-mt-1@sm u-ml-4@sm u-mb-8 u-mb-0@sm" id=toggle-issue-numbers>Show issue numbers</button></div><section class="c-updates u-is-displayflex u-flexvertical u-mb-10" data-latest-date><div id=1password-cli-2.42.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.42.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-11-04 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">November 4, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.42.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>The <code>op environment secret list</code> command is now generally available. It lists the name and value of each secret in a 1Password Environment, and whether each secret is concealed. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DEVAI-564'>#DEVAI-564</span></li><li>The <code>op environment</code> help text now uses &ldquo;secrets&rdquo; instead of &ldquo;variables&rdquo;. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DEVAI-291'>#DEVAI-291</span></li><li><code>op item get</code>, <code>op read</code>, <code>op run</code>, and <code>op inject</code> now return the value of an address field when some parts of the address, such as the street or country, are empty. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DI-1185'>#DI-1185</span></li><li>You can now authenticate the following CLIs using Touch ID and other unlock options with <a href=https://www.1password.dev/cli/shell-plugins>1Password Shell Plugins</a>. Thanks to everyone who contributed!<ul><li>CockroachDB CLI (<code>cockroach sql</code>), contributed by <a href=https://github.com/syndbg>@syndbg</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/536>shell-plugins#536</a></span></li><li>Doppler CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/CodeByZach>@CodeByZach</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/562>shell-plugins#562</a></span></li><li>DuckDB CLI with MotherDuck, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/sterlinm>@sterlinm</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/511>shell-plugins#511</a></span></li><li>LocalXpose CLI (<code>loclx</code>), contributed by <a href=https://github.com/LocalXpose>@LocalXpose</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/534>shell-plugins#534</a></span></li><li>Netlify CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/eddumelendez>@eddumelendez</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/627>shell-plugins#627</a></span></li><li>npm and pnpm, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/dalldrit13>@dalldrit13</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/658>shell-plugins#658</a></span></li><li>Octopus Deploy CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/xcezx>@xcezx</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/623>shell-plugins#623</a></span></li><li>OpenBao CLI (<code>bao</code>), contributed by <a href=https://github.com/gaige>@gaige</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/576>shell-plugins#576</a></span></li><li>Postman CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/ericflores108>@ericflores108</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/448>shell-plugins#448</a></span></li><li>Spacelift CLI (<code>spacectl</code>), contributed by <a href=https://github.com/damianstasik>@damianstasik</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/285>shell-plugins#285</a></span></li><li>Stackhero CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/martijngastkemper>@martijngastkemper</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/671>shell-plugins#671</a></span></li><li>xAI Grok CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/eddumelendez>@eddumelendez</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/626>shell-plugins#626</a></span></li></ul></li></ul><ul><li>The Argo CD shell plugin now respects the selected context: credentials from 1Password are only provided when <code>argocd</code> is targeting the server stored in the item&rsquo;s Address, so <code>--argocd-context</code> and <code>--server</code> work as they do without the plugin. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/678>shell-plugins#678</a></span></li><li>The Akamai and Pipedream shell plugins now refuse to write credential values containing line breaks into their generated config files. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/677>shell-plugins#677</a></span></li><li>The Exercism shell plugin no longer requires a 1Password item for the <code>completion</code>, <code>upgrade</code>, <code>workspace</code>, and <code>troubleshoot</code> subcommands. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/665>shell-plugins#665</a></span></li><li>The Sourcegraph shell plugin now supports the current <code>sgp_</code> access token format. The Endpoint field is now required, since each token is tied to a specific endpoint. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/marcleblanc2>@marcleblanc2</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/593>shell-plugins#593</a></span></li><li>The Hugging Face shell plugin now uses the new <code>hf</code> command instead of <code>huggingface-cli</code>. Run <code>op plugin init hf</code> and remove the old <code>huggingface-cli</code> alias. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/cadnza>@cadnza</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/573>shell-plugins#573</a></span></li><li>The Terraform shell plugin now provides credentials to <code>terraform output</code> and <code>terraform taint</code> commands. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/juraj-s>@juraj-s</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/556>shell-plugins#556</a></span></li><li>The LocalStack shell plugin now uses <code>LOCALSTACK_AUTH_TOKEN</code> instead of the deprecated <code>LOCALSTACK_API_KEY</code>. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/simonrw>@simonrw</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/428>shell-plugins#428</a></span></li><li>The MySQL shell plugin now quotes and escapes the values it writes to the generated <code>my.cnf</code>, so passwords containing <code>#</code>, backslashes, or surrounding whitespace no longer fail to authenticate. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/672>shell-plugins#672</a></span></li><li>The OpenTofu shell plugin now provides credentials to <code>tofu workspace</code> commands, matching the Terraform shell plugin. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/666>shell-plugins#666</a></span></li><li>The Gitea shell plugin now writes tea&rsquo;s configuration to the location tea reads when <code>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</code> is set. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/620>shell-plugins#620</a></span></li><li>The AWS shell plugin no longer fails with <code>Cannot call GetSessionToken with session credentials</code> when a profile with MFA assumes a role through a <code>source_profile</code>. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/684>shell-plugins#684</a></span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.41.1 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.41.1 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-10-21 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">October 21, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.41.1</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li><code>op read</code> help text now includes an example of reading a file attachment. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #TW-1440'>#TW-1440</span></li></ul><ul><li>Updated the CLI base image on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 to the latest hardened build to pull in security fixes. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #INFRASEC-1908'>#INFRASEC-1908</span> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #INFRASEC-1824'>#INFRASEC-1824</span></li><li>Updated Go to 1.26.10 to pull in the latest security fixes. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #INFRASEC-1824'>#INFRASEC-1824</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.41.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.41.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-10-12 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">October 12, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.41.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li><code>op run</code> now supports the <code>--environment</code> flag to load secrets from 1Password Environments. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #1461'>#1461</span></li></ul><ul><li>Reduced <code>op run --environment</code> network requests from 6 to 4. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DW-1414'>#DW-1414</span></li><li>Improved WASM performance of SDK-backed commands. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DI-1120'>#DI-1120</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.40.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.40.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-10-01 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">October 1, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.40.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>You can now trigger a Google Workspace user provisioning sync with <code>op provisioning google sync</code>. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #PROV-1718'>#PROV-1718</span></li><li>Accounts with no readable vaults no longer re-fetch the full vault list from the server on every command. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DI-817'>#DI-817</span></li><li>Accounts with 1Password Environments no longer re-fetch the full vault list from the server on every command. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DI-817'>#DI-817</span></li><li>Updated Go to 1.26.8 and the <code>golang.org/x/crypto</code>, <code>golang.org/x/net</code>, and <code>golang.org/x/text</code> modules to fix known security vulnerabilities. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DEVECO-364'>#DEVECO-364</span></li><li>Clarified in <code>op run</code> help text that secret masking on stdout and stderr is best effort and does not guarantee concealment. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DI-1088'>#DI-1088</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.39.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.39.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-08-14 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">August 14, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.39.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>Debug output now includes per-request timing. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #ECO-971'>#ECO-971</span></li><li>Debug output now reports more information when a vault cannot be read. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #ECO-817'>#ECO-817</span></li><li>Reporting item usage for cached items no longer delays reading secrets. Usage data is now sent in the background. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #ECO-970'>#ECO-970</span></li><li>A vault lookup that fails on the server is now reported as an error instead of incorrectly saying the vault isn&rsquo;t in the account. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #ECO-1017'>#ECO-1017</span></li><li>Connection error messages no longer include the full request URL, which could contain the account&rsquo;s email address. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #ECO-817'>#ECO-817</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.38.1 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.38.1 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-07-30 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">July 30, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.38.1</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>Reading an item with <code>op read</code> or <code>op item get</code> is now faster, using one fewer network round-trip per read. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #ECO-815'>#ECO-815</span></li><li>Reading an item or vault by name is now faster: <code>op read</code>, <code>op item get</code>, <code>op item list</code>, and <code>op vault get</code> use one fewer network round-trip when resolving a name. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #ECO-816'>#ECO-816</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.35.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.35.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-07-13 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">July 13, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.35.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>You can now authenticate the following CLIs using Touch ID and other unlock options with <a href=https://www.1password.dev/cli/shell-plugins>1Password Shell Plugins</a>. Thanks to everyone who contributed!<ul><li>Cline CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/eddumelendez>@eddumelendez</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/611>shell-plugins#611</a></span></li><li>CrateDB CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/accraw>@accraw</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/394>shell-plugins#394</a></span></li><li>Cursor CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/eddumelendez>@eddumelendez</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/612>shell-plugins#612</a></span></li><li>Descope CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/scottisloud>@scottisloud</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/570>shell-plugins#570</a></span></li><li>Exercism CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/dethancosta>@dethancosta</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/404>shell-plugins#404</a></span></li><li>Expo and EAS CLIs, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/CodeByZach>@CodeByZach</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/563>shell-plugins#563</a></span></li><li>GitHub Copilot CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/eddumelendez>@eddumelendez</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/603>shell-plugins#603</a></span></li><li>Google Gemini AI API CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/fproulx-boostsecurity>@fproulx-boostsecurity</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/560>shell-plugins#560</a></span></li><li>Jetbrains Junie CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/eddumelendez>@eddumelendez</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/604>shell-plugins#604</a></span></li><li>Kiro CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/eddumelendez>@eddumelendez</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/605>shell-plugins#605</a></span></li><li>OpenCode CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/eddumelendez>@eddumelendez</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/613>shell-plugins#613</a></span></li><li>OpenTofu CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/gargakshit>@gargakshit</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/553>shell-plugins#560</a></span></li><li>PyPI for twine, flit, and hatch, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/cpierce>@cpierce</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/589>shell-plugins#589</a></span></li><li>UpCloud CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/jksolbakken>@jksolbakken</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/538>shell-plugins#538</a></span></li></ul></li><li>The GitHub shell plugin now provisions <code>GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN</code> for GitHub Enterprise Server hosts and supports authenticating to both github.com and Enterprise when separate credentials are configured. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/scottisloud>@scottisloud</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/610>shell-plugins#610</a></span></li><li>The Redis CLI shell plugin now supports authenticating Redis CLI with environment variable-based provisioning. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/arunsathiya>@arunsathiya</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/276>shell-plugins#276</a></span></li><li>Tab completion is now supported when using shell plugins with bash and zsh shells. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #40'>#40</span></li><li><code>op</code> no longer hangs when running a shell plugin from outside <code>$HOME</code>. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/issues/416>shell-plugins#416</a></span></li><li>Terraform <code>workspace</code> subcommands now trigger authentication when using 1Password Shell Plugins. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/moraisph>@moraisph</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/582>shell-plugins#582</a></span></li><li>The Oh Dear shell plugin now checks for the <code>~/.ohdear/config.json</code> file and attempts to import credentials. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/owenvoke>@owenvoke</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/577>shell-plugins#577</a></span></li><li>The deprecated <code>zsh.initExtra</code> option has been replaced with <code>zsh.initContent</code> in the nix shell plugin. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/jbhannah>@jbhannah</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/550>shell-plugins#550</a></span></li><li>The awslogsCLI function has been renamed to capitalize CLI for consistency. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/518>shell-plugins#518</a></span></li><li>Deleting an invited or not-yet-activated user no longer fails on accounts with the Account Trust Log enabled. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #TRUST-862'>#TRUST-862</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.34.1 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.34.1 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-06-09 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">June 9, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.34.1</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>The <code>op vault edit</code> help text now better describes how the Travel Mode flag works. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #TW-1197'>#TW-1197</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.34.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.34.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-04-16 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">April 16, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.34.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>Authenticate the Claude Code CLI using Touch ID and other unlock options with 1Password Shell Plugins. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/malob>@malob</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/519>shell-plugins#519</a></span></li><li>Authenticate the Scaleway CLI using Touch ID and other unlock options with 1Password Shell Plugins. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/jksolbakken>@jksolbakken</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/515>shell-plugins#515</a></span></li><li>The AWS plugin now supports the <code>awslogs</code> CLI. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/jonasws>@jonasws</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/504>shell-plugins#504</a></span></li><li>The AWS plugin now supports <code>eksctl</code>, the Amazon EKS CLI. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/skpaz>@skpaz</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/500>shell-plugins#500</a></span></li><li>The AWS shell plugin now supports the AWS SAM CLI. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/simonmcc>@simonmcc</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/473>shell-plugins#473</a></span></li><li>The OpenAI shell plugin now supports the Codex CLI. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/shyim>@shyim</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/517>shell-plugins#517</a></span></li><li>The ngrok shell plugin no longer performs a version check on every <code>op plugin</code> command when it is not initialized. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/MOmarMiraj>@MOmarMiraj</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/474>shell-plugins#474</a></span></li><li>The AWS CDK shell plugin now supports AWS Profiles that assume a role when specified by the <code>--profile</code> flag. <em>Thanks <a href=https://github.com/waiteb3>@waiteb3</a>!</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/463>shell-plugins#463</a></span></li><li><code>op run</code> now properly terminates the subprocess it was called with when cancelled (for example, with Ctrl+C). <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #284'>#284</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.33.1 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.33.1 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-03-24 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">March 24, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.33.1</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li><code>op item edit</code> help text now includes a warning that JSON item templates don&rsquo;t support passkeys.</li><li>1Password CLI commands now support the Account Trust Log when the user authenticates with the 1Password desktop app.</li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.33.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.33.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-03-16 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">March 16, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.33.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>1Password CLI now supports updating an account&rsquo;s Account Trust Log when the feature is enabled.</li><li>The <code>--tags</code> flag on <code>op item edit</code> now replaces existing tags instead of appending them. An empty <code>--tags</code> value now properly clears all tags.</li><li>Empty tag strings in templates are now filtered out during <code>op item create</code> and <code>op item edit</code>.</li><li>Default values for <code>Date</code> and <code>MonthYear</code> fields are now unset instead of zero.</li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.32.1 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.32.1 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2026-02-05 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">February 5, 2026</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.32.1</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li><code>op item delete</code> help text now notes that deleted items remain in Recently Deleted for 30 days. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4377'>#4377</span></li><li>Tags are now deduplicated when using <code>op item edit</code>. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4088'>#4088</span></li><li><code>op run</code> help text now notes shell expansion order of operations. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #2971'>#2971</span></li><li><code>op item create</code> help text example now works without error. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4246'>#4246</span></li><li>1Password CLI now correctly exits with code 1 instead of 0 when encountering server error codes that are not recognized by the CLI. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #DG-682'>#DG-682</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.32.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.32.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2025-08-19 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">August 19, 2025</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.32.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>You can now use 1Password CLI to recover accounts for family or team members. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4161'>#4161</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.31.1 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.31.1 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2025-05-28 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">May 28, 2025</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.31.1</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>The 1Password app integration with 1Password CLI now works again on Windows. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4325'>#4325</span></li><li>A typo in the error message for &lsquo;op user confirm&rsquo; has been fixed. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4329'>#4329</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.31.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.31.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2025-05-07 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">May 7, 2025</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.31.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>1Password CLI no longer causes direnv to halt when the two are used together. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4250'>#4250</span></li><li>Following the deprecation of CLI 1, the <code>1password/op:latest</code> DockerHub tag will now always point to the latest version of CLI 2. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4267'>#4267</span></li><li>The Go version has been bumped to 1.23.8. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4305'>#4305</span></li><li><code>op vault list --filter</code> now returns all vaults you have access to regardless of permission level, making it easier to discover and manage vaults beyond those where you have read access. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4189'>#4189</span></li><li><code>op group user grant</code> now works correctly in MSP accounts. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4244'>#4244</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.30.3 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.30.3 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2024-11-07 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">November 7, 2024</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.30.3</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>The <code>OP_RUN_NO_MASKING</code> environment variable is now exposed to allow users to control the masking of the <code>op run</code> command output. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4089'>#4089</span></li><li>For 1Password accounts that are managed by an MSP, 1Password CLI commands involving Service Accounts, Connect, or the Events API no longer occasionally return an error. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4033'>#4033</span></li><li>The <code>op read</code>, <code>op run</code> and <code>op inject</code> commands no longer query archived items. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3893'>#3893</span></li><li>On Windows, the CLI now checks each signature of the 1Password desktop app before connecting to it. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4136'>#4136</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.30.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.30.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2024-07-31 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">July 31, 2024</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.30.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>Sensitive values in the human-readable output of item management commands are now concealed by default. You can display them using the <code>--reveal</code> flag. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4158'>#4158</span></li><li>Caching is now being used for service account sessions on Mac and Linux. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4133'>#4133</span></li><li>The error message when 1Password CLI can&rsquo;t connect with the 1Password desktop app now includes a link to troubleshooting documentation for more help. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3933'>#3933</span></li><li><code>op whoami</code> will now signal if the CLI is authenticated as a human user. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4104'>#4104</span></li><li>The output of <code>op vault list</code> now contains the created date and item count for each vault. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4092'>#4092</span></li><li>The <code>op item move</code> and <code>op item delete</code> commands now also work for SSH Key items. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3951'>#3951</span></li><li>The <code>op vault revoke user</code> command now doesn&rsquo;t allow you to revoke permissions in a Personal, Private, or Employee vault. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3844'>#3844</span></li><li>When the same environment variable name exists both in the operating system environment and an environment file, <code>op run</code> now correctly sources the value from the environment file. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3667'>#3667</span></li><li>The Windows Authenticode signature now uses the SHA256 hashing algorithm. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4135'>#4135</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.29.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.29.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2024-05-21 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">May 21, 2024</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.29.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>Team members can now use 1Password CLI to create service accounts when they have the required permissions to do so.</li><li>You can now use the <code>op whoami</code> command with a 1Password Connect server. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #2636'>#2636</span></li><li>Service account tokens now include device UUIDs for scalability purposes. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4009'>#4009</span></li><li>The output when you create a service account can now be formatted as a json object by adding <code>--format json</code> to the command. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3996'>#3996</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.28.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.28.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2024-05-01 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">May 1, 2024</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.28.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>Private vaults have been renamed Employee vaults for 1Password Business accounts. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3810'>#3810</span></li><li>1Password can now retrieve PKCS1-formatted SSH keys using <code>op read</code>. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3993'>#3993</span></li><li>The 1Password CLI package installed for macOS now correctly displays the CLI version in the package receipt. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #4027'>#4027</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.27.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.27.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2024-04-17 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">April 17, 2024</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.27.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li><code>op read</code> now outputs an error message consistent with the provided secret reference when no matching field or section is found on the item. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3592'>#3592</span></li><li>The output of SSH private keys now use platform-appropriate line breaks (CR vs CRLF). <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3913'>#3913</span></li><li>Users who have the <code>manage_vault</code> permission in a vault can now grant and revoke access to the vault. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3863'>#3863</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.26.1 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.26.1 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2024-03-22 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">March 22, 2024</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.26.1</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>The CLI build for Darwin now builds with Go 1.21.8. The previous version was built using an older version, which was causing alerts for certain customers.</li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.26.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.26.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2024-03-19 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">March 19, 2024</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.26.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li><code>op service-account create</code> command allows you to create a new service account that you can use to automate secrets management.</li><li><code>op service-account ratelimit</code> command allows you to fetch information about service account rate limit usage. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3886'>#3886</span></li><li><code>op user provision</code> now clarifies that users will not be considered for billing until they accept their invitation. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3965'>#3965</span></li><li><code>--expires-in</code> flags now support days and weeks. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3298'>#3298</span></li><li>The <code>item share --expiry</code> flag is now aliased to the standardized <code>--expires-in</code> flag. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3298'>#3298</span></li><li>We corrected a typo in the <code>user suspend</code> error message. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3298'>#3298</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.25.1 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.25.1 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2024-03-12 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">March 12, 2024</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.25.1</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>We&rsquo;ve fixed an issue retrieving an SSH Key when using 1Password CLI with a Connect server. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3851'>#3851</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.25.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.25.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2024-02-26 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">February 26, 2024</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.25.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li><code>op vault list --permission</code> now allows you to retrieve a list of vaults for which a user or group has specific permissions. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3879'>#3879</span></li><li>When setting a non-generated password, 1Password CLI now always correctly updates the password strength. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3787'>#3787</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.24.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.24.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2023-12-14 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">December 14, 2023</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.24.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>The 1Password CLI Mac installer now allows for custom location selection. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3731'>#3731</span></li><li>Help text now uses present tense more consistently where actions in the present are described. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3768'>#3768</span></li><li>Help text now refers to the 1Password app consistently. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3626'>#3626</span></li><li>Help text now refers to Connect server instances and tokens consistently. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3476'>#3476</span></li><li><code>op group user grant</code> and <code>op group user revoke</code> no longer panic when the group doesn&rsquo;t exist. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3859'>#3859</span></li><li>Duo MFA is no longer prompted for more often than required. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3907'>#3907</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.23.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.23.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2023-11-16 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">November 16, 2023</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.23.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li><code>op item edit</code> now accepts JSON input via the <code>--template</code> flag. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #1849'>#1849</span></li><li><code>op item edit</code> now supports piping items as JSON via stdin. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #1849'>#1849</span></li><li>If you&rsquo;re not an owner and try to add the Team Members group to a vault when the <code>limitedGroupVaultAccess</code> feature flag is turned on, 1Password CLI now returns a helpful error. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3830'>#3830</span></li><li>When 1Password CLI can&rsquo;t connect to the 1Password desktop app, the error message now suggests restarting the app. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3835'>#3835</span></li><li>We&rsquo;ve improved the error message when <code>op item edit</code> finds duplicate fields to more clearly format field labels that aren&rsquo;t in a section. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3849'>#3849</span></li><li>Creating a vault with <code>--icon=name</code> now works again, using the updated icons. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3833'>#3833</span></li><li>The error message for <code>op item edit</code> when duplicated fields are found by label no longer prints the field&rsquo;s value. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3848'>#3848</span></li></ul></div></article><div id=1password-cli-2.22.0 class=u-anchor-offset>&nbsp;</div><article class="c-updates__release u-mb-6"><header class="c-updates__header u-is-displayflex u-aligncenter u-p-4 u-px-6@md"><a href=#1password-cli-2.22.0 class="c-updates__anchor fal fa-link u-is-displayblock"><time datetime="2023-10-24 00:00:00 +0000 UTC" class="c-heading c-updates__date u-mb-2 u-is-displayblock">October 24, 2023</time><h6 class="c-heading c-updates__title">1Password CLI 2.22.0</h6></a></header><div class="c-updates__content u-py-8 u-px-4 u-px-8@md"><ul><li>You can now authenticate the following CLIs using Touch ID and other unlock options with 1Password Shell Plugins. Thanks to everyone who contributed!<ul><li>Axiom CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/rajapri28613>@rajapri28613</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/342>shell-plugins#342</a></span></li><li>Binance CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/bala-ceg>@bala-ceg</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/391>shell-plugins#391</a></span></li><li>Civo CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/itsCheithanya>@itsCheithanya</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/296>shell-plugins#296</a></span></li><li>Crowdin CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/JoeKarow>@JoeKarow</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/359>shell-plugins#359</a></span></li><li>HuggingFace, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/bala-ceg>@bala-ceg</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/393>shell-plugins#393</a></span></li><li>InfluxDB CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/bala-ceg>@bala-ceg</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/392>shell-plugins#392</a></span></li><li>Flyctl CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/arunsathiya>@arunsathiya</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/141>shell-plugins#141</a></span></li><li>Kaggle CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/rajapri28613>@rajapri28613</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/341>shell-plugins#341</a></span></li><li>LocalStack CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/simonrw>@simonrw</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/371>shell-plugins#371</a></span></li><li>MongoDB Atlas CLI , contributed by <a href=https://github.com/joqim>@joqim</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/198>shell-plugins#198</a></span></li><li>Pipedream CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/rajapri28613>@rajapri28613</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/338>shell-plugins#338</a></span></li><li>Todoist CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/rajapri28613>@rajapri28613</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/340>shell-plugins#340</a></span></li><li>Upstash CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/siddhikhapare>@siddhikhapare</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/316>shell-plugins#316</a></span></li><li>Vertica CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/parthiv11>@parthiv11</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/327>shell-plugins#327</a></span></li><li>Yugabyte CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/parthiv11>@parthiv11</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/322>shell-plugins#322</a></span></li><li>Zapier CLI, contributed by <a href=https://github.com/rajapri28613>@rajapri28613</a> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/337>shell-plugins#337</a></span></li></ul></li><li>We&rsquo;ve updated help text for many commands to use simpler language. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3676'>#3676</span> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3768'>#3768</span></li><li><code>op read</code> help text now includes an example of how to use the <code>ssh-format</code> query parameter to get an SSH key&rsquo;s private key. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3795'>#3795</span></li><li><code>op run</code> help text now includes an explanation of how to use service accounts with <code>op run</code>. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3804'>#3804</span></li><li>We&rsquo;ve updated error messages for <code>op item create</code> to be more clear. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3766'>#3766</span></li><li>We&rsquo;ve updated error messages when provisioning actions fail to be more clear. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3263'>#3263</span></li><li><code>op whoami</code> for service accounts now authenticates automatically instead of asking to authenticate the service account token. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3744'>#3744</span></li><li>The PostgreSQL shell plugin now supports <code>pgcli</code> as an alternative to <code>psql</code>. <em>(Thanks, <a href=https://github.com/szymon>@szymon</a>!)</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/384>shell-plugins#384</a></span></li><li>The Cachix shell plugin now checks for the <code>~/.config/cachix/cachix.dhall</code> file and attempts to import an auth token using the specified file. <em>(Thanks <a href=https://github.com/dethancosta>@dethancosta</a>!)</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#shell-plugins#373</span></li><li>The Sentry CLI shell plugin now skips authentication when you use the <code>--auth-token</code> and <code>--api-key</code> flags. <em>(Thanks <a href=https://github.com/roy9495>@roy9495</a>!)</em>. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/370>shell-plugins#370</a></span></li><li>The Homebrew shell plugin now provides authentication for the <code>upgrade</code>, <code>update</code>, <code>install</code> and <code>reinstall</code> commands. <em>(Thanks <a href=https://github.com/cullenmcdermott>@cullenmcdermott</a>!)</em>. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#shell-plugins#369</span></li><li>The Sentry shell plugin now supports <code>SENTRY_PROJECT</code> & <code>SENTRY_URL</code>. <em>(Thanks <a href=https://github.com/JoeKarow>@JoeKarow</a>!)</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#shell-plugins#363</span></li><li>The PostgreSQL plugin now also supports the <code>pg_dump</code> and <code>pg_restore</code> CLI utilities. <em>(Thanks <a href=https://github.com/JoeKarow>@JoeKarow</a>!)</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/353>shell-plugins#353</a></span></li><li>The OpenAI shell plugin now has updated documentation and management URLs. <em>(Thanks <a href=https://github.com/arunsathiya>@arunsathiya</a>!)</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/351>shell-plugins#351</a></span></li><li>When generating the shell plugin template, you now only need to set the last word of the credential name as the default 1Password field name if the credential name is longer than seven characters. <em>(Thanks <a href=https://github.com/arunsathiya>@arunsathiya</a>!)</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#shell-plugins#263</span></li><li>The ngrok shell plugin now specifies the correct credential length. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/250>shell-plugins#250</a></span></li><li>The ngrok shell plugin now uses environment variables in ngrok version 3.2.1 and later. <em>(Thanks <a href=https://github.com/arunsathiya>@arunsathiya</a>!)</em> <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab'><span class=sr-only>Git reference </span>#<a href=https://github.com/1Password/shell-plugins/pull/222>shell-plugins#222</a></span></li><li>We&rsquo;ve restored deprecated JSON keys for <code>op whoami</code> output for service account for backwards-compatibility. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3754'>#3754</span></li><li><code>op whoami</code> now throws the appropriate error if an invalid service account token is set. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3744'>#3744</span></li><li>When you search for an item by title and vault and the title is 26 characters long, 1Password CLI now returns the item. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3751'>#3751</span></li><li><code>op vault list</code> now only returns vaults you have read access to. <span class='c-icon c-icon--gitlab' role=img aria-label='Git issue #3688'>#3688</span></li></ul></div></article></section></div></section><section class="c-panel c-panel--overflow-hidden c-filter-footer c-filter-footer@md u-pt-16 u-pt-24@md"><div class=c-panel__container><div class="u-text-sm u-text-md@md u-text-center u-mb-0"><h6 class="c-heading c-heading--1 u-mb-8 u-mb-16@md">1Password works everywhere</h6><img src=/img/works-everywhere.ac528b46f7ae7bcf3ac7f4c10ece50a3.svg class="o-image o-image--centre u-mb-12 u-mb-16@md" alt><div class="c-filter-footer__platforms u-is-displayflex u-flexwrap u-flexnowrap@md u-mx-auto u-alignstart@md"><a href=/mac/ class="c-filter-footer__platform u-is-displayblock c-filter-footer__platform-link c-filter-footer__platform-link@md u-is-displayflex u-flexvertical u-aligncenter u-mb-12 u-mb-20@md"><div class=u-is-displayflex><div class="c-filter-footer__platform-icon-wrapper c-filter-footer__platform-icon-wrapper@md"><img src=/img/icons/mac.c9ebce467fb349f702480deeb30e1ed4.svg class="c-filter-footer__platform-icon c-filter-footer__platform-icon@md u-mb-2" alt></div></div>Mac
